    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμίξ</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mixedly, confusedly,
			pell-mell</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἵπποι τε καὶ</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.525
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				21.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. δέ τε μαίνεται
			Ἄρης</span> Ares rages <i>without</i>
			<i>respect of persons</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.537
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. κτείνονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.60
				</span></i>
			: in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Wi.</u>
				14.25
			</span></i>.</div>
